# The rotten scaffolding on the tower's north-west side (prop vrt_scaffolding): a back way in, to a hole broken through the
# wall of the third floor, the lantern room (Dungeon Expansion Plan V1; Elven Tower, chapter 11). It goes in by a
# conversation so the hunter's-tower quest moves as it does at the door.

~ climb
Narrator: Grey, split planks lash the north-west wall with sodden rope, climbing in crooked stages toward a jagged hole at the third floor. None of the timber looks happy about its work.
* Climb the rotten scaffolding toward the hole above. -> up
* Step back and leave the scaffolding alone. -> END

~ up
if guest:ezmerelda and not flag.rictavio_gone and (not quest.the_hunters_tower or quest.the_hunters_tower == heard or quest.the_hunters_tower == asked)
quest the_hunters_tower with_her
elif tarokka.ally.npc != ezmerelda and (not quest.the_hunters_tower or quest.the_hunters_tower == heard or quest.the_hunters_tower == asked)
quest the_hunters_tower inside
endif
Narrator: Every wet plank groans under your boots until you haul yourself through the broken masonry. The room inside smells of copper and a storm that has not broken yet.
time +10
move van_richtens_tower_interior:lantern_from_scaffold
